**THE AXES — recommend SIX: ATK · PEN · HP · DEF · SPEED · RANGE.** All six are fields the engine reads for every unit. ⛔ I recommend AGAINST attack-speed as a seventh/sixth because two entries in the table are fabrications (chewer 300 legacy, drone 60 "unused placeholder"). If the owner wants attack speed anyway it is still ZERO sim change — derive it display-side as `chewsConnectors ? CHEW_INTERVAL_TICKS : attackCadenceTicks`, skip `selfExplode` units, and invert (`minCadence / cadence`). Put that to him rather than guessing.

**NORMALISATION — GLOBAL, and I recommend it without reservation.** One shared max per axis across the whole roster is exactly what produces the effect he described ("a bat 1,1,1,1… Vlad mega developed"). Per-axis-relative would rescale every card and make a bat and Vlad look identical, which is the opposite of the ask. Derive the maxima from `CREATURE_CONFIGS` + `DEFENDER_CONFIGS` at module load — today HP 24 · DEF 16 · ATK 10 · PEN 10 · SPEED(maxAccel) 240 · RANGE 420 — so a retune moves the chart automatically and nothing new lands in the canon.

